{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Vinc sidecar HTTP contract",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The HTTP routes of the Vinc sidecar (api/server.py) and the account routes the desktop and web app (app/) call. Paths are the ones the app passes to its data plane: the desktop shell calls them on the loopback sidecar with the session bearer, web Vinc reaches the same graph operations under /api/graph on the account, and desktop account mode sends them through POST /space/proxy. Only paths and methods are pinned here; request and response bodies are not.\n\nx-served-by: 'sidecar' is a route in api/server.py; 'account' is served by the account backend and never by the sidecar.\nx-internal: true means the app does not call the operation; other callers (MCP bridge, CLI, hub entrypoint, embedding worker, account proxy) may. false means app/src or the shell in app/src-tauri calls it.\n\nChecked by tests/core/test_sidecar_contract.py (every sidecar route is listed, every listed sidecar operation is a route) and app/dev/sidecar-contract-check.ts (every call the app makes is listed and not internal, every listed non-internal operation is called). OPTIONS answers CORS preflight on any path and is not listed."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:{port}",
      "description": "Loopback sidecar started by the desktop shell.",
      "variables": {
        "port": {
          "default": "8787",
          "description": "Port the shell hands over through sidecar_conn; 8787 is only the fallback."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "sidecarToken": []
    }
  ],
